  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Essential Support to Private Households in Kherson and improving their capacity to prepare for winter</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Save UA Foundation conducted the needs assessment of the population of the affected areas in southern Ukraine and decided to focus on preparation for the winter period and decided to focus on supporting a small number of communities (2 communities) with a more comprehensive approach for 6 months, with the possibility of extension.  We established strong cooperation links with oblast and local authorities, consolidated territorial communities affected areas and systematically update their needs and accept requests for assistance. SaveUA also organized a hotline, which helps to understand how the situation changes in real time. According to assessment conducted, SAVE UA propose to provide support for 2 hromadas, both in de-occupied Khersonska oblast: Vysokopillya hromada and Stanislavska hromada.</narrative>
  </description>
